Thanks to PVSnesLib
-------------------

The kit's console API (lib/include/sdevkit/snes.h) took the interface of PVSnesLib
(https://github.com/alekmaul/pvsneslib, MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2012-2026 alekmaul) as its
model: the functions, their parameters and their meaning follow PVSnesLib's, under names of the
kit's own. superdevkit contains no code of PVSnesLib; the implementation is the kit's own. We are
grateful to alekmaul and PVSnesLib's contributors for the work this builds on.


Images
------

The picture docs/assets/Dampf.jpg and the design of the splash logo (dev/art/LogoLarge.png)
were generated with Google's Nano Banana image model (Gemini image generation). The splash logo
is made from dev/art/splash/logo_source.png, a version of that design the author edited by hand.


Software from third parties
---------------------------

This product includes software from third parties:

- The ANTLR 4 runtime (org.antlr:antlr4-runtime 4.13.2), shipped in the distribution as
  java/antlr4-runtime-4.13.2.jar, and the code ANTLR generates into dampf's parser.
  Copyright (c) 2012-2022 The ANTLR Project. BSD licence, text below.

- The C grammar compiler/src/main/antlr/dampf/parser/CLexer.g4 and CParser.g4, from
  antlr/grammars-v4 (https://github.com/antlr/grammars-v4), commit
  754339a6bf1e8e622fdce4e26dc846baee603ff4, and the parser dampf's jar contains that is generated
  from it. Copyright (c) 2013 Sam Harwell. BSD licence, text below.

- The parser support classes in compiler/src/main/java/dampf/parser/ (CLexerBase, adapted,
  and CParserBase, Symbol, SymbolTable, TypeClassification), from the same commit of
  antlr/grammars-v4 (c/Java/), written by Ken Domino and the other contributors of grammars-v4.
  At that commit these files carry no licence notice of their own. The changes to them are
  listed in compiler/src/main/antlr/dampf/parser/README.md.

- In the release zips, a Java runtime in jre/: OpenJDK as Eclipse Temurin 25.0.5+8, cut down with
  jlink and unmodified otherwise. GNU General Public License v2 with the Classpath Exception; the
  licence texts are in jre/legal/. The source of exactly this build is the archive
  OpenJDK25U-jdk-sources_25.0.5_8.tar.gz at
  https://github.com/adoptium/temurin25-binaries/releases/tag/jdk-25.0.5%2B8

- In the release zips, raylib 5.5 (https://github.com/raysan5/raylib) in raylib/, ready-built
  from raylib's own releases. zlib licence; the text is in the LICENSE file of each folder there.


